From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 06:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pluginadapter: post toasts as transient (light) notifications

Every toast event-monitor's plugins post is a status blip - "Wi-Fi
network is connected", "Wired LAN cable disconnected", pdm's USB device
events. On LuneOS the shell keeps any toast that does not declare
type "light" as a sticky entry in the notification area, so each of
these lingered until the user swiped it away; connecting to Wi-Fi
should not leave homework behind.

Declare the type in the one place all plugin toasts pass through, so
they show as the transient banner popup only. Plugins needing a
persistent notification should use createAlert, or grow an explicit
parameter here.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS specific]
---
 src/service/pluginadapter.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/src/service/pluginadapter.cpp
+++ b/src/service/pluginadapter.cpp
@@ -418,6 +418,10 @@
 	params.put("message", JValue(message));
 	params.put("sourceId", JValue(this->manager->lunaService.servicePath + "-" +
 	                              this->info->name));
+	// Status blips, not tasks: "light" keeps them as the transient banner
+	// popup only, instead of also parking a sticky entry in the shell's
+	// notification area that the user has to swipe away.
+	params.put("type", JValue("light"));
 
 	if (iconUrl.length() > 0)
 	{
